      "request": {
        "description": "Measure the compiled official MuJoCo model, nominal IK feasibility, contact behavior, and matched 10-substep action/braking responses before selecting a learning direction.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "args": [
              "--output",
              "campaigns/evaluations/b9d3f752-0619-4863-81cc-96c7df3918d4/physics_baseline.json"
            ],
            "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/b9d3f752-0619-4863-81cc-96c7df3918d4/physics_baseline.json",
            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "compiled physics and matched response baseline",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.physics_baseline"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial scientific distinction is whether the first goal gap should be attributed to learned control/hold behavior or to compiled inertia, solver/contact, or actuation semantics. Nominal geometry alone cannot resolve that distinction. This deterministic PI-owned measurement directly records compiled options and effective mass, analytic branch residuals and conditioning, joint-limit margins, contacts, and substep trajectories under saturated and zero actions from the singular start and valid IK branches. Outcomes that show contact or unexpected authority/solver behavior would redirect early work toward physical/semantic investigation; a contact-free nominal model with adequate bidirectional braking would support treating future failure as a policy/control capability problem and selecting training/evaluation accordingly."
      },
